    "explanation": "Malfurion tends to do well on Maps that feature many choke points, as he can easily get value from Entangling Roots there, and on Maps where team fights are not extremely long, as he would end up having Mana issues.\n\nIn general, however, his versatility makes him a solid pick on most Maps. Team compositions should be the most important factor to consider when drafting Malfurion because not having any protection from allied Heroes may be a problem."
  },
  "builds": [
    {
      "name": "Nature's Balance Build",
      "label": "Recommended",
      "description": "Malfurion's Nature's Balance Build makes it easier to hit enemy Heroes with Moonfire and to keep Regrowth active on allied Heroes in the late game.\n\nRejuvenation at Level 4 is important to have when you are the only Healer in your team. When that is not the case, you can replace it with either Celestial Alignment for more damage or with Shan'do's Clarity to enable an allied Hero with more Mana and cooldown reduction.\n\nNature's Swiftness at Level 13 drastically increases your survivability, however, it can occasionally be replaced with Hindering Moonfire when facing Heroes who can be kited (such as Garrosh) or with Revitalize when you need more Mana.",
